Set 17: Core Web Vitals: INP Optimization in Complex SPAs

Mercor Primary Question: "How do you measure, debug, and optimize Interaction to Next Paint (INP) on dynamic enterprise dashboards?"

Mercor Follow-up Probe: "Break down the three phases of an interaction under INP. Where does the majority of enterprise UI delay occur?"

Model Answer:

INP measures the longest latency between a user interaction and the next visual browser frame update.

Addressing the probe: The three phases are:

Input Delay: Waiting for background tasks to clear before the event handler runs.

Processing Duration: Time spent executing the JavaScript event handler.

Presentation Delay: Time required for the browser to recalculate styles, layout, and paint the next frame.

In complex ERP dashboards, Presentation Delay is usually the primary bottleneck due to massive DOM trees. We optimize INP by offloading heavy filtering to Web Workers, debouncing high-frequency triggers, and using yieldToMain (via scheduler.yield() or microtask breaks) before triggering DOM writes, allowing the browser to present visual feedback immediately.

